	(text "R1/R2 (5.1k on CC1/CC2): only fit them if your USB-C breakout does not already have them.\nTP4056 (protected) boards: battery goes to B+/B-, load to OUT+/OUT-. B- and OUT- are NOT the same net (the protection FET is between them).\nMT3608: turn the trimmer to ~5.1 V with a multimeter BEFORE connecting the Pi."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 252 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "22f95f6d-f8ec-4e21-8b49-131b92c849c8")
	)
	(text "DIY iPod - electronics (Pi Zero 2 W + PCM5102A + ILI9341 + MPR121 touch wheel)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "31dfe196-92e1-46c5-b176-a8422f664f7c")
	)
	(text "TOUCH CONTROLLER + WHEEL (I2C)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 55.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "370d266a-91fa-4112-9eec-3dc6b5a2fab4")
	)
	(text "PCM5102A (GY-PCM5102 style) solder pads: FLT=L, DEMP=L, XSMT=H, FMT=L. SCK is tied to GND (internal PLL). Jack is on the module.\nLCD VCC and DAC VIN come from 5 V (both modules have an on-board regulator) so the backlight does not load the Pi's 3V3 pin. MPR121 runs from 3V3.\nPi /boot/firmware/config.txt:  dtparam=i2c_arm=on   dtparam=spi=on   dtoverlay=hifiberry-dac"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 266 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3acf9fdd-bced-4b57-b1c9-aaee78ed54ec")
	)
